CAPTURED, NOT CHASED -- litK's literal and emitLeaf's disagree

litK spells the literal as `term.tag` for every term. emitLeaf bakes `node.text`,
which planTerm sets to `term.text` when the term carries string data and to
`term.tag` when it does not. For a data-carrying literal term the two generators
therefore match DIFFERENT text. litToK copies litK deliberately, so the twin
agrees with its sibling rather than hiding the divergence behind a third
spelling. Banked as a row in docs/fixIts.md the day this landed. It predates this
remedy and is not repaired by it.

